    <section class="am-tajweed-syllabus section-padding">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="section-heading text-center mb-50">
                <span>Curriculum &amp; Details</span>
                <h2>Online Tajweed Course Syllabus</h2>
                <p>A step-by-step curriculum that moves from letter sounds to confident Quranic recitation.</p>
                <img src="assets/img/icons/title.ico" alt="" />
            </div>
            <div class="am-tajweed-group-title"><span>01–04</span><h3>Key Tajweed Rules Covered</h3></div>
            <div class="row g-4 mb-5">
                <div class="col-lg-3 col-md-6"><article class="am-tajweed-card am-tajweed-rule"><span class="am-tajweed-number">01</span><h3>Makharij</h3><p>Study the articulation points of Arabic letters and learn where each sound originates: the throat, tongue, lips or mouth.</p></article></div>
                <div class="col-lg-3 col-md-6"><article class="am-tajweed-card am-tajweed-rule"><span class="am-tajweed-number">02</span><h3>Sifaat</h3><p>Understand letter characteristics such as heaviness, lightness, strength and softness, and how they shape each sound.</p></article></div>
                <div class="col-lg-3 col-md-6"><article class="am-tajweed-card am-tajweed-rule"><span class="am-tajweed-number">03</span><h3>Noon Sakin &amp; Tanween</h3><p>Learn Izhar, Idghaam, Iqlaab and Ikhfaa, including when to make a clear, merged or nasal sound.</p></article></div>
                <div class="col-lg-3 col-md-6"><article class="am-tajweed-card am-tajweed-rule"><span class="am-tajweed-number">04</span><h3>Meem Sakin</h3><p>Practice the rules of Meem Sakin and learn how to pronounce it correctly in different letter combinations.</p></article></div>
            </div>
            <div class="am-tajweed-group-title"><span>05–10</span><h3>Advanced Tajweed Rules</h3></div>
            <div class="row g-4">
                <div class="col-lg-4 col-md-6"><article class="am-tajweed-card am-tajweed-rule"><span class="am-tajweed-number">05</span><h3>Idghaam</h3><p>Learn how a sound is joined or merged with the letter that follows it during recitation.</p></article></div>
                <div class="col-lg-4 col-md-6"><article class="am-tajweed-card am-tajweed-rule"><span class="am-tajweed-number">06</span><h3>Iqlaab</h3><p>Understand when and how a sound changes according to the Iqlaab rule.</p></article></div>
                <div class="col-lg-4 col-md-6"><article class="am-tajweed-card am-tajweed-rule"><span class="am-tajweed-number">07</span><h3>Ikhfaa</h3><p>Practice partially concealing a sound while keeping its required nasal quality.</p></article></div>
                <div class="col-lg-4 col-md-6"><article class="am-tajweed-card am-tajweed-rule"><span class="am-tajweed-number">08</span><h3>Madd</h3><p>Study elongation rules and learn how to stretch sounds for their correct duration.</p></article></div>
                <div class="col-lg-4 col-md-6"><article class="am-tajweed-card am-tajweed-rule"><span class="am-tajweed-number">09</span><h3>Stopping Rules</h3><p>Read common Quranic stopping signs and identify suitable places to pause.</p></article></div>
                <div class="col-lg-4 col-md-6"><article class="am-tajweed-card am-tajweed-rule"><span class="am-tajweed-number">10</span><h3>Starting Rules</h3><p>Learn how to resume recitation correctly after a pause while maintaining meaning and flow.</p></article></div>
